Manual Endpoint Testing

Before running load tests, manually test the endpoints.

Test Unpaginated Endpoint
curl -w "\nTime: %{time_total}s\nSize: %{size_download} bytes\n" \
http://localhost:3001/api/quotes/unpaginated
Test Paginated Endpoint
curl -w "\nTime: %{time_total}s\nSize: %{size_download} bytes\n" \
"http://localhost:3001/api/quotes?page=1&limit=20"
Test POST Endpoint
curl -X POST http://localhost:3001/api/favorites \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{"quoteId":1}'
Installing Artillery

Install Artillery globally:

npm install -g artillery

Verify installation:

artillery version
Load Test Configuration

Create a file named:

load-test.yml

Example configuration:

config:
  target: "http://localhost:3001"

  phases:
    - duration: 30
      arrivalRate: 50
      rampTo: 50
      name: "Ramp up to 50 users"

scenarios:
  - name: "Get all quotes (unpaginated)"
    flow:
      - get:
          url: "/api/quotes/unpaginated"

  - name: "Get paginated quotes"
    flow:
      - get:
          url: "/api/quotes?page=1&limit=20"

  - name: "Add to favorites"
    flow:
      - post:
          url: "/api/favorites"
          json:
            quoteId: 1
Running the Load Test

Execute:

artillery run load-test.yml
Important Metrics
Median Response Time
50% of requests are faster than this value
Gives a general performance overview
p95 Response Time
95% of requests complete within this time
Represents the slowest user experiences
Most important metric for scalability analysis
Throughput

Measured in:

requests/second

Shows how many requests the server can handle.

Error Rate

Percentage of failed requests:

500 errors
timeouts
failed responses

High error rates indicate server overload.

Expected Findings
Unpaginated Endpoint

Expected to show:

Higher response times
Increased memory usage
Lower throughput
Worse p95 latency

Because the server returns all 1,000 quotes in one response.

Paginated Endpoint

Expected to show:

Lower response times
Better throughput
Smaller payload sizes
Improved scalability

Because only 20 records are transferred per request.

Hidden Issues You May Discover

The starter project intentionally contains performance and implementation issues such as:

Missing CORS handling
Chunked transfer problems
Pagination off-by-one errors
Synchronous blocking operations
Missing input validation